    "title": "<p>Conventional histopathological patterns and differential diagnoses of cutaneous Kaposi sarcoma (KS)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Wayne Grayson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 545.15pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"727\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.85pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"200\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histopathological pattern</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Differential diagnoses</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"200\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Patch-stage KS</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Early microvenular haemangioma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Interstitial granuloma annulare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mild inflammatory dermatosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"4\" valign=\"top\" width=\"200\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Plaque-stage KS</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Microvenular haemangioma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Tufted angioma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Targetoid haemosiderotic haemangioma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Acroangiodermatitis (pseudo-KS)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.85pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"8\" valign=\"top\" width=\"200\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Nodular KS</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Vascular tumours composed of spindled cells (e.g. spindle cell haemangioma, Kaposiform haemangioendothelioma, angiosarcoma)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Kaposiform lymphangiomatosis (including cellular pattern)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dermatofibroma subtypes (e.g. cellular, aneurysmal, haemosiderotic, atypical)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Angiomatoid fibrous histiocytoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"PT\">Spindle cell sarcoma (e.g. dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans, leiomyosarcoma)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Spindle cell amelanotic melanoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 14; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dermal fasciitis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 15; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 395.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"527\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Bacillary angiomatosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
