    "title": "<p>Less common histopathological patterns and differential diagnoses of cutaneous Kaposi sarcoma (KS)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Wayne Grayson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 703.3pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histopathological pattern</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Differential diagnoses</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Anaplastic (pleomorphic) KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Spindle cell sarcoma (e.g. leiomyosarcoma, malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumour, spindle cell rhabdomyosarcoma, fibrosarcoma, fibrosarcomatous dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Amelanotic spindle cell melanoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Spindle cell carcinoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"4\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Lymphangioma-like (lymphangiomatous) KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Lymphangioma (e.g. acquired progressive lymphangioma, lymphangioma circumscriptum)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Kaposiform lymphangiomatosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Postradiation atypical vascular proliferation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Angiosarcoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Lymphangiectatic <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">KS<sup>a,b</sup></span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Lymphangioma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Telangiectatic <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">KS<sup>c</sup></span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intratumoural congestion and ectasia of native (i.e. non-neoplastic) blood vessels</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Sinusoidal haemangioma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Bullous <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">KS<sup>b</sup></span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Re-epithelializing subepidermal bulla unrelated to KS </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Cavernous haemangioma&ndash;like <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">KS<sup>c</sup></span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Cavernous haemangioma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Hyperkeratotic (verrucous) <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">KS<sup>b</sup></span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Verruciform epidermal hyperplasia and hyperkeratosis unrelated to underlying KS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 14; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Keloidal KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">True keloid scar (e.g. arising at a previous punch biopsy site for confirmation of KS)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 15; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Micronodular KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Early intradermal spindle cell sarcoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 16; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Early cellular dermatofibroma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 17; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pyogenic granuloma-like KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pyogenic granuloma (lobular capillary haemangioma)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 18; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Bacillary angiomatosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 19; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Ecchymotic KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Intradermal haemorrhage/ecchymosis due to another cause (e.g. biopsy-related trauma)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 20; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"5\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intravascular KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intravenous pyogenic granuloma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 21; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intravascular papillary endothelial hyperplasia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 22; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intravascular fasciitis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 23; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 24; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intravascular myopericytoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 25; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Angiomatous KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Haemangioma (e.g. sinusoidal, spindle cell)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 26; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Cellular angiolipoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 27; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Glomeruloid <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">KS<sup>d</sup></span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Glomeruloid haemangioma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 28; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Tufted angioma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 29; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">KS with myoid <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">nodules<sup>c</sup></span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans with myoid nodules</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 30; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pigmented KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intralesional haemosiderin pigment deposition in a neoplasm other than KS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 31; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Melanocytic proliferation (e.g. spindle cell melanoma, cellular blue naevus)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 32; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pigmented dermatofibrosarcoma protuberans (Bednar tumour)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 33; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Regressing/regressed KS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Inflammatory dermatosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 34; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 511.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"683\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Dermal neovascularization</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-no-proof: yes;\">a</span></sup><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-no-proof: yes;\">Lymphangiomatous</span><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\"> KS may be associated with bullous lesions clinically, hence forming part of the clinical spectrum of bullous KS. <sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">b</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Lymphangiectatic,</span> bullous, and hyperkeratotic (verrucous) KS may be associated with chronic lymphoedema, hence forming part of the clinical spectrum of lymphoedematous KS. <sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">c</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Telangiectatic KS,</span> cavernous haemangioma&ndash;like KS, and KS with myoid nodules are usually associated with background features of classic nodular KS. <sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">d</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Glomeruloid</span> KS probably forms part of a morphological continuum with angiomatous KS.</span></p>",
